        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/feather_sound_florida"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mangroves, salt marshes, and open water once covered Feather Sound, but 20th‑century dredging and infill reshaped the shoreline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/feather_sound_florida"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Orange Belt Railroad reached the Feather Sound area in the 1880s, opening the interior for homesteading.",
